  "query_preview": "..  (Friday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 329 AM CDT Thu May 21 2026\n\nThe LREF is continuing to show that the upper flow will stay out of \nthe southwest through next week with a number of upper troughs \nmoving through the area at the same time.  The two most notable \ntroughs at this point look to move across the CWA on Sunday and \nTuesday when 40-60% of the LREF members are producing rain across \nthe area.  It should be noted that least 20-30% of the members are \nproducing some rain each period, particularly over the southeast \nhalf of the CWA which will be closer to a surface front that remains \nstalled under the southwesterly flow.  \n\nTemperatures will slowly warm up closer to normal over the weekend \ninto next week as the LREF is showing a ridge building over the \nMidwest.  While we should see some increase in temperatures, the \nwarmup should be tempered by the clouds and rain chances and not as \nhigh as the NBM which is on the warmest side of the temperature \nguidance. \n\nBritt",
